From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 03:53:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: apple-dart: let a T8132 external DCP power its
 firmware DART down

An external DCP (dcpext) powers its firmware DART down with
apple_dart_dcp_power_off(), idle with nothing attached and for a deep
sleep, as the internal DCP does when blanked. apple_dart_dcp_consumer()
only finds a DART that has its clock-protection slice, and the slice is
looked up for the internal display DARTs alone. The J604 DT names the
dcpext firmware DARTs' slices (5 and 30), but on 1.873 both dcpexts log
"idle: power-down not possible now: DART (-19)" and never power down.

Look the slice up for the dcpext firmware DARTs too. The external display
DARTs (dispext) stay excluded: they go down with their display.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
index 62ee206eea..c4496ed2cf 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
@@ -5214,8 +5214,15 @@ static int apple_dart_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	dart->preserve_display = j713_display || j713_dcpext || j713_dispext;
 	dart->dispext = j713_dispext;
 	dart->power_gated = j713_dispext;
-	if (j713_display && of_property_present(dev->of_node, "apple,clock-protection")) {
-		/* Its DCP can power it down: see apple_dart_dcp_power_off(). */
+	/*
+	 * The internal display DARTs and the external DCPs' firmware DARTs:
+	 * their DCP can power them down (apple_dart_dcp_power_off()), the
+	 * internal one when blanked, an external one idle with nothing attached
+	 * or for a deep sleep. Without the slice apple_dart_dcp_consumer() finds
+	 * no DART and every external DCP power-down is refused (-ENODEV).
+	 */
+	if ((j713_display || j713_dcpext) &&
+	    of_property_present(dev->of_node, "apple,clock-protection")) {
 		dart->ps_prot = syscon_regmap_lookup_by_phandle_args(dev->of_node,
 								     "apple,clock-protection",
 								     1, &dart->ps_prot_slice);
-- 
